abstract: >-
  An open book of executed Jupyter notebooks, with a small Python module, on
  asymptotic methods for scientists and engineers: asymptotic expansions and
  divergent series, and the asymptotic evaluation of integrals and sums
  (Watson's lemma, Laplace's method, stationary phase, steepest descent,
  Euler-Maclaurin), with worked examples from chemical physics and heat
  transfer. Every expansion is checked against high-precision numerics.
